Game profiles: each process picks its FIFA workarounds by its main exe's name.

CX_DR_TRAP, CX_TOPDOWN_LIMIT and CX_FIFA16_DSTFIX were bottle-wide
environment variables, so one bottle could only be set up for one game. The
community launchers (Aurora.exe, Impulsum17, CAS, RebornFUT) start several
FIFA games out of one bottle, and each game then ran with the launcher
bottle's settings: FIFA 15 in an Aurora17 bottle got FIFA 17's CX_DR_TRAP=2
and no CX_TOPDOWN_LIMIT, and died with 0x80000004.

cx_profile_init (unix/loader.c) runs once in start_main_thread, right after
init_startup_info has the main exe's name and before any guest code, and
resolves all three settings for the process. Per setting the first layer
that says anything wins: HKCU\Software\Wine\AppDefaults\<exe>\CrossOver-FIFA
"DrTrap"/"TopdownLimit"/"Fifa16DstFix"; the same key's "Profile"
(fifa15|fifa16|fifa17|fifa21|none); the built-in table (fifa15.exe,
fifa16.exe, fifa17.exe, _fifa17.exe, fifa21.exe, fifa21_trial.exe, any case);
the bare environment variable, as before; off. A profile sets all three,
including the ones it turns off. Processes the table does not name --
launchers, WebView2, .NET helpers -- get the bare variables exactly as before.

The three readers (drbp_mode, the dst fix, NtAllocateVirtualMemory's top-down
limit) no longer cache: they ask cx_dr_trap/cx_fifa16_dstfix/cx_topdown_limit,
which answer from the bare variables until the profile is resolved, so a
signal taken before then cannot pin a process to its bottle's value. Those
are parsed once, first thing in start_main_thread (or on the first call, if
anything is earlier), into statics of their own: no getenv per signal. An
empty AppDefaults value counts as not there. When a
profile resolves to mode 3 and the bottle-wide variable did not, the second
view of KUSER_SHARED_DATA that mode 3 reads through is mapped then.

PF_PAE_ENABLED lives in KUSER_SHARED_DATA, written once per session by the
process that boots it, so it cannot be per-exe: CX_PF_PAE=1 turns it on for
the session, and a bare CX_DR_TRAP=3 still does too.

CX_GAME_PROFILES=0 ignores the table and the registry: the old behaviour.
WINEDEBUG=+cxprofile logs one CXPROFILE line per process. Applies after every
other patch (dlls/ntdll/unix only).

